A6.4 -- what a PER-PIXEL sigma_F would do, bounded by the ladder
==============================================================================
  A uniform rescale is priced exactly by the linear-gate identity. A
  per-pixel sigma_F is not a uniform rescale, and this arm cannot price
  it -- doing that needs a merge whose tolerance varies per pixel, which
  is a change under crates/ and outside M69's brief. What CAN be bounded
  is the range: run the ladder at 4*p05 and 4*p95 of each stack's own
  per-pixel rho distribution and read how far n_eff travels.

